\pard\plain \tx960\fi960\sl360\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f2\fs24\b1\i0 Neural swaps,}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0  with respect to humans are quite difficult. As with the brain our memories which inadvertently form our personality traits are often made up of grey matter. In short memories are physically made up in the brain, therefore a brain swap cannot essentially take place with two different brains, ruling this out. However in the sense of the sentient their brains are malleable, meaning consciousness can be swapped although not the other way around. The relationship is therefore set out like this in the Serva Vitae Universe. }
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b1\i0  Sentient to Human bridge. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 The memories of the sentient are all but disbanded in the sentient shell as the sentient takes hold of the human sleeve. The sentient can experience the humans memories all the same, without the consciousness of it\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s own past, it merely acts as a pilot to the shell, incapable to reflect on it\u8217\'92s own purpose and aligned with the humans memories and moral compass. It\u8217\'92s own memories are stored and banked in it\u8217\'92s data banks within it\u8217\'92s own shell. This means that Sentients may be able to bridge to a human mind but forgetting their past and main objectives. }
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b1\i0 Human to Sentient Bridge. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 As the Sentient brain is malleable, formed off the scans of it\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s host when it was created. The material within a sentient brain is malleable. Formed by the orchestrated scans of it\u8217\'92s designer and eventual targeted human. It is due to this that sentient\u8217\'92s face the vulnerability of commandment by human counterparts. . }}